Why bother with something as drastic as rewriting all the code for interaction
on the game level.  I propose a simple magic portal in between lev 10-15 that
warps you to a tavern/arena/bazaar.  I envision it as rather like the Bazaar
at Deva, from the Robert Asprin series "Myth...".
You step on a magic portal --- more ---
You feel dizzy for a moment but it passes --- more ---
Hello, Conan!  Welcome to Ingrids tavern --- more ---
The Groom takes your large dog named Cthulu --- more ---
That will cost you 10 gold to stable --- more ---
Scumwise says Hi! --- more ----
<#c>
which direction?  --- more ----
<7>
What would you like to say to scumwise?  --- more ---
<Hello!>
You say Hello! to Scumwise.
<#c, 9, hi>
Ingrid says, say "Buy" if you want to see my wares.
<#c, 9, Buy>
What would you like to purchase?  Etc...
Hule appears in a puff of smoke 
Hule throws a dagger --- more ---
the dagger hits you --- more ---
You have been challenged to a fight to the death!  --- more ---
You are escorted to the arena --- more ----
Your wand of death is taken from you --- more ----
"Fight"
Hule hits!  Hule hits.  Hule Hits!
<a, 23, 9>
Status of Hule:  Neutral  (300) 450p  (23) 30mp  10150 g.
You die.  --- more ---
Your wand is given back to you --- more ---
You feel drained.  --- more ---
You are now level 14 --- more ---
Hule seems more experienced.

	I also imagine a couple of shops, and maybe a quest on that level.

